# Pier architecture
Source of truth: blueprints/00-plan.md plus approved blueprints (01-foundation.md).
- Cross-platform Rust app (Windows, macOS, Linux); PierOS distro is optional packaging of the same binary.
- Cargo workspace under crates/: api-types (serde DTOs shared by server and web, WASM-safe), core (Docker via bollard, topology, no HTTP), server (axum REST + WebSockets, stream hub on tokio broadcast), traffic (eBPF via aya, Linux-only, feature-gated), web (Rust/WASM UI with Leptos; three.js 3D map via JS interop). gRPC (tonic) later on top of core.
- Crate package names use the pier- prefix (pier-core, pier-api-types, pier-server, pier-web); folders are crates/<name>.
- One install manages exactly one Docker host; no host ids in routes or core types.
- Auth: single admin user now; users table with role column so roles can be added later without redesign.
- Docker connection is configurable: Unix socket, Windows named pipe, TCP+TLS, SSH.
- core returns domain DTOs, never raw bollard types; no HTTP or DB deps in core.
- server: axum, sqlx SQLite store, argon2 sessions; binds 127.0.0.1:8640 by default.
- Keep designs minimal; update this file and ask other rule owners to update theirs when architecture changes.
